\newlabel{bounded-search-diagnostics}{{6.5}{16}{Bounded-search diagnostics}{subsection.6.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Response to a persistent hotspot introduced after a feasible warm-up. The dashed line marks slot 51, when the hotspot is imposed and then held fixed. (a) Slot-wise satisfaction and (b) slot-wise migration count, with means and 95\% bootstrap bands across 30 paired runs per scenario. Admission and rejection transitions are excluded from both migration measures.}}{17}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Minimum component ablation under the same persistent-hotspot protocol. (a) Full method minus variant post-onset satisfaction. (b) Post-onset migration count and (c) migration-volume proxy. Points and whiskers in (a) are paired means and 95\% bootstrap intervals; bars in (b,c) are run means across 30 seeds per scenario.}}{17}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces BudgetedLNS uses a bounded search neighborhood and rarely reaches its 5\% local-search trial guard. (a) Candidate evaluations per slot. (b) Recorded accepted reconfiguration moves per 200-slot run. (c) Budget-active slots per 200-slot run. Boxplots and faint points show run-level distributions; diamonds and whiskers are arithmetic means and deterministic 95\% bootstrap intervals over 30 frozen runs per scenario. These diagnostics describe observed search behavior and do not identify a causal decomposition.}}{18}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
